(Consider the Lilies -- Sister Amelia Vance, October 2025) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (I want to speak this morning about the ordinary work of noticing.) Tj
T* (It is easy to believe that ministering is a program with a form to) Tj
T* (fill in. It is not. It is the practice of paying attention to the) Tj
T* (people who sit near you, week after week, until you know them.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (When the Savior taught his disciples to consider the lilies, he was) Tj
T* (not asking them to admire a flower. He was asking them to notice how) Tj
T* (thoroughly they are provided for, and to let that noticing change how) Tj
T* (they carried their worry.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (I have watched this ward do that quietly for years. A meal left on a) Tj
T* (step. A ride to an appointment nobody advertised needing. These are) Tj
T* (not small things dressed up as large ones. They are the thing itself.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (May we continue to notice one another, and may we be slow to mistake) Tj
T* (activity for attention.) Tj
